So, it finally happened! To be honest, I didn't expect an ascension
this soon. I've only played maybe 60ish games total, and this was my
40th game on NAO. After reading about all the folks who had played for
years and never ascended, it kind of came to me as a surprise that I
was able to ascend on my first run where I managed to make it to
Medusa. I admit, I have spoiled myself as much as possible(maybe too
much... I spent a lot of time idling and looking up a lot of stuff to
decide exactly what I needed for my ascension kit) and I felt like I
had some VERY LUCKY early game breaks. What helped me the most were
the 2 posts I made here on rgrn. I asked for some help with what I now
know was a very trivial situation involving a vampire and then another
post about getting killed by a Green-Elf with a wand of sleep. I
received all sorts of useful feedback and got some wonderful advice! I
must say, I was pleasantly surprised with the enthusiasm and kindness
of the community here compared to other gaming communities. You all
really made me feel welcome.

I decided to ditch the pet on the first level and never really had one
after that....I guess I don't regret my decision. I did come back up
to lvl 1 once to discover buc status of some items so he served his
purpose well enough. When I start playing a wizard, I'll bet I find it
hard to imagine living without a pet. I just felt confident in the
Valks beatdown abilities and figured I could pick up a pet later if I
needed to. I generally went with the "explorer" strategy - clear out
each level of its loots fully and move down. There was a general store
on level 2 that I used a few times to price id stuff which I found out
later had a scroll of genocide and a ring of levitation(that I wasted
a wish on haha). Level 3 gave me the stair-down to mines and a chaotic
altar which I soon converted. I found an elven mithril-coat early
which was nice. I picked up a ring of conflict that confused the heck
out of me for a while until I finally figured out what it was lol. I
explored down to maybe level 5 or 6 and then started sacrificing on
the altar on level 3 for awhile(the altar was right next to some
stairs, ended up hauling some rothe/cave spider corpses up the stairs
to sac). I found a +4 orcish helm which put me at -6 AC and level 7. I
was pretty pumped with this nice of an early start.

I proceeded down to the mines where I picked up telepathy off a
floating eye. The luck really hit me when the mine level before
minetown was a bones level, and had a sparkly SDSM in his inventory,
as well as tons of cursed goodies. I had to make a lot of trips just
to carry all the loot to the minetown altar. I just spend tons of time
sorting out and priceid'ing as much of this stuff as I can.

I eventually left Minetown after doing a lot of loot sorting and
uncursing(and id'ing everything with a lucky blessed ident scroll)with
-17 AC at level 9. This was easiest the best I had been doing at this
early of a point in the game. I decided I was going to be very patient
and careful, while taking my time to make decisions. Of course I
always try to do this, but at this point, I was finding myself playing
with my inventory/stash far longer than I normally do and spending
more time to make my decisions. Watching my ttyrec would probably be
very boring cuz I know I stood at my stash at different parts for 1-2
hours at a time lol.

I went back up to some earlier fountains and got Excalibur. I then
headed to Sokoban and got my bag of holding(perfect since I had my
SDSM). From there I headed back to minetown to sort out more loot. I
ended up making many trips to the fountain pools and to the coaligned
altar to blank some scrolls and make some holy water. I FINALLY head
to Mine's end at level 11 with -18 AC around turn 12000(I told you I
like to waste time!). I'd say that from here on out, nothing really
threated my life very much. Mine's end was quick and painless. My AC
gradually grew to the high -20s when I got more protection from
sacrificing and spent some money at the priest. I've never had AC near
this low in previous games and I was impressed at how invulnerable I
was to melee in general.

I headed back to my altar on level 3 and did more sacrificing until I
acquired Frost Brand. I quickly figured out that you can't dual-wield
artifact swords lol! I guess that would be a bit overpowered... ;)

I decided I was read to move on down and plow through everything in
sight(ok, I wasn't that confident at that point lol)! I cleared the
big room with ease and found an altar down on level 20. I wasted a lot
of time here sacrificing with no real point(I guess I was hoping for
that artifact sabre) as I didn't pray much at all....should I have
been trying to get crowned at this point?

I did another run back to my Minetown stash. Wasted a lot of time
here. I brought a few things back and started a new stash on level 20.
I killed Medusa with ease and kept pushing down. I hit 14 and decided
it was time to do the quest for the first time! It was, as expected, a
pushover. It was certainly a fun break though and I'm greatly looking
forward to the quests for the other classes. After that, I AGAIN went
allll the way back to minetown to do some more loot sorting and armor/
weapon enchanting. I then did some mass scroll blanking/potion
diluting and made enough holy waters that lasted me through the rest
of the game. I'm wondering if there aren't better ways to manage my
stash rather than having to run all the way back to minetown so many
times as I did this game. I did eventually move my stash to level 20
but I still ended up going back to there once before doing my
ascension run as I forgot a magic marker that I was gonna charge.

I got to the castle and cleared it out with ease. I was still 14 at
this point with -22 AC. Nothing seemed to dent me at all. It took me a
bit to figure out how to get the drawbridge to come down, but I never
figured out how to get it to come down after that lol. I ended up
falling into a bit into(what I didn't know at the time) the Valley of
the Dead. I ended up clearing most of it before finding the upstairs
back to the castle. I used my wand of wishing to get 2 scrolls of
charging, ring of levitation, gauntlets of power, boots of speed,
cloak of magic resistance and an amulet of life saving(I wanted all
the help I could get!!!). I did more enchanting and was ready to
plunge down to hell at level 19 with my +6 frost brand, +6 silver
saber and -29 AC. I also decided it'd be a good idea to genocide L.
The kind folks here on rgrn told me that I was ready for Gehennom so I
took the plunge!

With my new toys and enchantments I really tore the place up. The
silver saber made it especially brutal for the poor denizens. Nothing
too exciting except for the wand of wishing I found. Nothing really
threatened me and I proceeded to clear all the way down to the
vibrating square(I didn't do anything with the wizard's towers yet).
It took me forever to find the square and I ended up taking my pick-
axe and tearing up the whole place, FINALLY finding it. Hopefully it
won't be so painful next time! I probably would've found it quicker
had I realized it was the bottom level and I could've avoided cutting
all the corners and just making sure to step on each square while
exploring.

I marked the vib square and decided to head all the way back up to my
stash, and do my final preparations. I believe I ended going back to
minetown one last time as I forgot some things somehow hahaha. I used
my wand of wishing on another wand of death, some magic markers and
genocided master mind flayers, mind flayers, and R(a disenchanter took
my weapons down to +5 which annoyed me at the time but I later
realized it was a blessing as I got my weapons both up to +7...I just
wanted to get that threat out of the way, maybe there was a better
choice). After spending lots of time debating over whether I was
prepared, I finally went down to meet the Wizard, and begin the run.

It took me a bit to figure out how to find Wizard's tower, but now I
got it figured out and it should be quick next time. I killed the
Wizard easily, and made a mad dash down to the vib square. The Wizard
said hello to me once right after I performed the invocation and I
zapped him with my wand of death. I decided to take the advice of some
of the spoilers I read and try to insta-gib him anytime he appeared.
In the end he cursed one of my rings once and that was all. I cleared
out Murloch's Sanctum, took down the high priestess and yanked the
Amulet. I proceeded upstairs as quickly as possible(having
teleportitis/control made this nice). I stopped at my stash on level
20 and checked everything over. I had a charge left on my wand of
wishing and decided I would bring it along incase I needed anything. I
was quickly up to the planes and I think I killed the wizard another 1
or 2 times on the way. The planes went pretty smooth as I brought some
potions of confusion, and some cursed/uncursed scrolls of gold
detection. I found the portals quickly and was proceeding quickly. The
air elementals on the plane of air did more damage to me than anything
else in the game at any other point in the game. I was never in much
danger, but they really brought my health down. I probably should have
taken more time to kill the monsters slowly instead of trying to make
a mad dash to the portal and getting practically surrounded. I just
took my time and did eventually fight them all off without having to
use any sort of escape method or potion. I finally got up to the plane
of water. Here I noticed all of these silly ; monsters. I thought that
I should turn easy-mode on and genocide them right there on the spot
as I knew the Astral Plane was just up ahead. I wrote up a scroll of
genocide and poof, the level was pretty much cleared. It took me a bit
to find the portal up even after reading my scroll of gold detection
and spotting it.

Up into the Astral Plane I went! I pulled out my fresh wand of death,
some wands of teleportation, my K-rations and my potions of full
healing. I decided to take off my ring of free action and put on
Regeneration/Slow Digestion. I wasn't sure if I would need Free Action
or not, but figured I wanted the slow digestion for Famine(who I was
headed to first). I used my telepathy to locate Pestilence, Death and
Famine. Pestilence was on the far left so I decided I'd try the right
altar first. Famine was the first out the far right door and he died
to the first zap from my wand of death. I tried to break a wand of
teleportation to clear out the packed door and ended up confused just
as Famine came back from the dead and touched me. I zapped him again
with the wand of death and I missed. For some stupid reason(not sure
why I did this lol), on my next turn I attacked a summoned killer be
while Famine touched me again, making me weak from hunger. I got
REALLY scared at this point, and ate a K-Ration. I decided to just
swing at Famine on my next turn and he once again dropped to the
floor. I spotted a hole between the mobs at the door and made my way
closer to the right altar. It looked like the altar was aligned so I
was relieved that I didn't have to deal with Pestilence. It was very
clumped right outside the altar room and I broke another wand of
teleportation to clear some space. It didn't work that great and
really made me ponder how useful boots of jumping might have been. I
had some great spots where I could've jumped into a single square
ahead of the pack. I plowed through the monsters in front of me(well,
they did get me down to 200/280) and finally made it in the temple. I
stepped up to the altar and did a little jig.

I'm really looking forward to playing more classes and eventually
trying some conducts. There is still so much fun to be had!! Here's
